{
 "file": "13- Interpersonal Communication Skills.docx",
 "title": "Interpersonal Communication Skills",
 "duration": "3 Days",
 "overview": [
  "The success of an organization hinges on the team members' capacity to engage in communication through various means and channels. Our interactions with others play a pivotal role in shaping perceptions, making each interaction an opportunity to fulfill a planned purpose. Effective communication stands out as a potent skill for accomplishing objectives, whether at a personal or organizational level. This training program is designed to equip you with the necessary skills to focus on your purpose, understand your audience, and craft a clear message for optimal impact and outcomes. Creating an atmosphere conducive to open discussion and continual dialogue is paramount for achieving success in communication"
 ],
 "audience": [
  "Individuals in search of enhancing their communication proficiency, including employees, supervisors, managers, and others aiming to refine their skills both within the workplace and in various personal contexts"
 ],
 "methodology": [
  "This course utilizes self-analysis questionnaires to enable participants to discover and apply their preferred communication methods with others. Furthermore, the use of case studies, round table discussions, and role plays ensures that the course content is comprehensible and readily applicable"
 ],
 "competencies": [
  "Verbal and non-verbal communication",
  "Influencing others",
  "Assertiveness",
  "Active listening",
  "Building rapport",
  "Networking and providing feedback",
  "Conflict management"
 ],
 "objectivesIntro": [
  "By the end of the course, participants will be able to:"
 ],
 "objectives": [
  "Apply effective communication skills",
  "Demonstrate cross-cultural communication abilities",
  "Utilize techniques for active and empathic listening",
  "Manage interpersonal conflicts",
  "Handle feedback and criticism constructively"
 ],
